044 - Morning Has Broken
 / 
Key: C
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 44
Topic: Worship - 

Verse 1:
[C]Morning [Em/B]has [Am]broken Like [G/B]the [Am/C]first [G/B]morning,
[C/G]Blackbird [G7/F]has [Dm]spoken [C]Like the first [G]bird.
[G]Praise [C/G]for [G]the [C/E]singing! Praise for the [D7/F#]morning!
[Em/G]Praise for [G]them [Am/E]springing Fresh [C/G]from [G7/F]the [C/E]Word!

Verse 2:
[C]Sweet the [Em/B]rain's [Am]new [Dm/A]fall [Am]sunlit from [G/B]heaven,
[C/G]Like the [G7/F]first [Dm]dewfall [C]on the first [G]grass.
[G]Praise [C/G]for [G]the [C/E]sweetness of the wet [D7/F#]garden,
[Em/G]Sprung in [G]completeness [C/G]where His [G7/F]feet [C/E]pass.

Verse 3:
[C]Mine is [Em/B]the [Am]sunlight! Mine [G/B]is [Am/C]the [G/B]morning
[C/G]Born of [G7/F]the [Dm]one [C]light Eden saw [G]play!
[G]Praise [C/G]with [G]elation, [C]Praise every [D7/F#]morning,
[Em/G]God's recreation [Am]of [C/G]the [G7/F]new [C/E]day!
